A||N||4||Xtreme Fiero's||towing a lowered Fiero and bushing/mount question||||5||
Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||10-18-2000||11:23 PM||||<BR>I hope to get my first V6 Fiero inside the next month, a 1985 GT that needs a new trans. it is lowered and I don't think a two wheel car dolly will work to tow it near 400 miles. and I don't know how to get it up on a trailer with one or mabye two peopple pushing it. any one got any ideas?<P>while I have the cradle out I will also put in a set of alu. bushings. should I reuse the stock mounts or get Poly trans & motor mounts or it the dog bone enough?<P> I slaped together a few pic's of the car I hope ot buy, though I am haveing some trouble geting in touch with the curent owner.<P> <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/XTREME_KUSTUMZ/doc" TARGET=_blank>http://community-2.webtv.net/XTREME_KUSTUMZ/doc</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Hank is Here||10-19-2000||12:25 AM||||My best advise is a block and tackle or a hand crank boat winch to get it on a trailer. You may even be able to rent a come-a-long for a few bucks fo the day too and use that, though it should be rated at least 1000 pounds.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||10-19-2000||02:51 AM||||My second Fiero was an 86GT that had ST lowering springs and 50 series tires on 15 inch rims.  The thing is basically on the ground.  It was running (but leaking oil like a well), so I towed it home on a car transport.  It was so low that to get it onto the transport, I had to disconnect the trailer from my hitch and jack the front of the trailer up in the air so the car wouldn't scrape at the top of the ramps.  It still did and I was afraid that I would get hung up in the middle somewhere.<P>I just towed a real pathetic Fiero 120 miles on a really pathetic tow dolly.  It was really an easy trip.  I don't think I would worry about how far you are going.  It just seemed a lot easier that the whole transport thing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||10-19-2000||08:34 AM||||I can get a car dolly N/P but I don't want to beat the crap out of the front end by graging it 400 miles om a bumpy/ bridge infested road. my main consert with the full trailer is getting hung up at the top of the ramps||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hank is Here||10-19-2000||08:09 PM||||Okay if you are worried about the facia hitting the ramps on the front that is a really easy fix.  Just get two 8" wide 36" long boards.  Place those on the ground and about 1/2 way up the ramp.  This softens the angle,  I do this trich all the time on rollback trucks and have gotten really low riders on without a problem, hell even the owners are suprised on how I load them.||||reg||14
